=== ES8311 sample-rate sweep ===

regs  : the clock registers read back off the chip over I2C

lrck  : the frame clock MEASURED against the kernel cycle counter,

        which is not derived from the I2S clock

adc   : the microphone noise floor with the amplifier off. A running ADC

        returns a dithering floor; a zero one means the codec's clock tree

        did not come up -- OR that its analog was disturbed less than ~6 s

        ago and its reference caps are still charging (HW-023). This cannot

        tell those apart, so a zero floor is not by itself a fault.

order : the rates ASCEND, and so does time, so a settling effect and a rate

        effect are confounded in any run that starts from a disturbed codec.

        Reading a low-rate cliff off this table without reversing it first is

        exactly how 'the reset deafens the ADC below 22 kHz' was invented.

tone  : the captured level with the amplifier on. Reported, not

        asserted: this speaker couples weakly into this microphone.

        Judge the speaker by ear; the pitch rises across the sweep

        because the tone table was made for 16 kHz


